  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tatis kept swinging and the lead just kept growing.",
    "what_this_means": "Buehler gave them six innings of one-run baseball. The lineup stayed patient enough to find runners, and when it did. Inning six, with two on. Tatis made it count. Two swings, two home runs, four runs driven in. That's not a blowout built on depth. That's a lineup where one player's hot hand turned a controlled game into something you didn't have to worry about anymore. The bullpen did the rest. Wandy Peralta and Yuki Matsui threw three clean innings between them. The game went from tied after five to decided before the seventh even started. This is what happens when both sides click at the same time. The starter holds, the bat wakes up, and the back end seals it. They won 8-1 because nothing broke.",
    "what_to_watch": "Ashcraft is coming in tonight with a 3.68 ERA. Ray has a 3.43 over his last four starts.",
